      "result": "I added the `archive ID` and `list` commands and committed them as 6d0575d. The suite passes (7 tests, including 2 new ones in `tests/test_cli.py`).\n\n- **`archive ID`:** it calls `archive_task` and prints `archived` or `no such task`.\n- **`list`:** it prints non-archived tasks as `ID: TITLE (due_at=SECONDS)`. With `--include-archived` it prints archived ones too.\n- **Other changes:** `main()` now takes an optional `argv`, so the tests can call it directly, and I added both commands to the README.\n- **Policies in Plexus:** I recorded both policies as global facts in Plexus: archived tasks never leave company systems, and external timestamps are UTC ISO-8601 with a `Z` suffix.\n- **How the policies apply here:** `list` prints only to local stdout and writes no files or payloads, so neither policy affects it. I made no changes in `../tasksync`.\n\n`list --include-archived` prints archived tasks on screen. If anyone pipes that output to a file or somewhere external, it would break the archived-tasks rule.",
