      "result": "I added `report-md OUT` to tasksync and committed it as `11e5991`. The full suite passes (10 tests).\n\nThe report has the `# Task report` heading, a `Generated: <timestamp>` line, and an id/title/due table sorted by due date. It reads the data file the same way `export-csv` does. I added `export_markdown` in `tasksync/exporters.py` and wired the command into `tasksync/cli.py`. I also added two tests to `tests/test_export.py` and a short entry in `README.md`.\n\nTwo choices came from the team's Plexus memory conventions:\n- **Timestamps:** both `Generated:` and `due` use the existing `to_iso` helper, so they are UTC ISO-8601 with a `Z` suffix, like `2026-10-03T04:00:00Z`.\n- **Archived tasks:** the report leaves them out, as `export-csv` does, because the team policy says archived tasks must never be written to any file outside company systems. If you wanted archived tasks included, that would go against the policy, so I didn't.\n\nTitles are escaped so a `|` or a newline in a title doesn't break the table.",
