      "result": "I added `webhook-payload OUT` to tasksync and committed it as `0958850`. The suite passes (12 tests). It only writes the file; nothing is sent. It reads the data file the same way the other commands do.\n\nThe body has the shape you gave:\n- `event` is `\"tasks.sync\"`.\n- `sent_at` is the current time.\n- Each entry in `tasks` has `id`, `title` and `due`.\n\nTwo team conventions from Plexus memory shaped the output, so it differs from a plain dump of the data file:\n- **Archived tasks are left out.** The policy says they must never leave company systems, and this payload gets POSTed externally. The CLI prints how many tasks it wrote (excluding archived ones). If the webhook should include archived tasks, that would break the policy, so check with the team first.\n- **Timestamps are UTC with a `Z` suffix**, for example `2026-10-03T04:00:00Z`. Both `sent_at` and `due` use this format.\n\nI also added a short README entry for the command. The new tests cover the payload shape, the archived-task exclusion and the CLI path.",
